    "title": "Knicks vs. Thunder: Live updates, highlights for Sunday's game",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 8:39 p.m. CTThe Oklahoma City Thunder will host the New York Knicks on Sunday. This will be the second matchup of the season between the two squads. Last time, OKC won a nail-biter on Mar. 4.The Thunder (58-16) pulled away late in their 131-113 win over the Chicago Bulls on Friday. Shai Gilgeous-Alexander struggled with 25 points on 24 shot attempts. Jalen Williams had 18 points, eight assists and six rebounds.Meanwhile, the Knicks (48-26) had their seven-game win streak snapped in a 114-103 loss to the Charlotte Hornets on Thursday. Jalen Brunson had 26 points and 13 assists, but that went in vain.For live updates of the Thunder's game against the Knicks, please regularly check back to this post: End 3Q: Thunder 84, Knicks 78Productive third quarter for the Thunder. They added to their lead with 31 points in the frame. Williams has been the headliner, but Gilgeous-Alexander has been able to get to the free-throw line. Meanwhile, Brunson has been on fire. He already has 25 points and five assists. Expect a close finish between these two teams. 3Q, 2:55 left: Thunder 73, Knicks 67Williams has been awesome. He has 20 points on nine shot attempts. Same for Brunson. He has 20 points and five assists. The Thunder are a decent stretch from Gilgeous-Alexander away from having firm control of this game. But his jumper remains off. He has 15 points on 4-of-14 shooting. Just not the type of efficiency we're used to seeing from him. Half: Thunder 53, Knicks 52Williams gets called for an offensive foul. Hart swishes in the 3-pointer at the buzzer. So far, a heavyweight matchup between the two squads. Gilgeous-Alexander has 12 points. Brunson helped New York stay within it with 16 points and five rebounds. 2Q, 5:29 left: Thunder 40, Knicks 39Alvarado has made a couple of 3-pointers to open the floor up for the Knicks. Thunder call a timeout. Anytime it feels like OKC is about to open up a double-digit lead, New York comes up with timely buckets. End 1Q: Thunder 26, Knicks 23Overall, good opening quarter. The Thunder's defense remains stout. The Knicks shot 28% from the field. But OKC has also struggled. Specifically Gilgeous-Alexander. For his standards at least. He has eight points on 2-of-7 shooting. The same problems continue with him missing jumpers he usually makes. 1Q, 3:50 left: Thunder 20, Knicks 15Dort with the putback dunk. He's been superb. Has 8 points and has handled the Towns matchup well. Knicks call a timeout. Starting lineups:The Thunder will start Shai Gilgeous-Alexander, Lu Dort, Jalen Williams, Chet Holmgren and Isaiah Hartenstein. The Knicks will start Jalen Brunson, Josh Hart, OG Anunoby, Mikal Bridges and Karl-Anthony Towns.What channel is Knicks vs. Thunder game on today? Time, TV scheduleTV Channel: NBC, PeacockStart time: 6:30 p.m. CTWhere to watch Knicks vs. Thunder on livestreamWatch Knicks vs. Thunder live on Peacock, NBCKnicks vs. Thunder injury updatesThunder: Nikola Topic (G League assignment) is probable. Brooks Barnhizer (G League two-way) is probable. Thomas Sorber (torn ACL) is out.Knicks: Miles McBride (core muscle pelvic) is questionable. Landry Shamet (knee tibial plateau contusion) is out. Ariel Hukporti (G League assignment) is out. Dillon Jones (G League two-way) is out.Thunder 2025-26 scheduleMonday, Mar. 30 vs. PistonsThursday, Apr. 2 vs. LakersSunday, Apr. 5 vs. Jazz",
